---
import BaseEn from '../../layouts/BaseEn.astro';
---
<BaseEn title="Privacy Policy — OneTech Solutions" description="How OneTech Solutions handles your data and your customers' data: minimum permissions, an isolated environment per client, and no selling of data.">

	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</div>
			<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
			<p>We work with your business data and your customers' data, so we write down plainly what we collect, how we use it, and what your rights are. Last updated: November 2026.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>What we collect</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				What you give us directly when you reach out or in a discovery session (your name, your business, your contact
				channel, and a description of your daily process), and the operational data needed to build and run your
				automation (such as the order or appointment records the system we build for you processes).
			</p>

			<h2>How we use it</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li>To deliver the service agreed in the written offer: building, running and monitoring your automation.</li>
				<li>To prepare the before/after reports we use to measure results with you.</li>
				<li>To contact you about your project and agreed support.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Our standing principles</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li><b>Minimum permissions:</b> we never ask for access the service does not need.</li>
				<li><b>An isolated environment per client:</b> your data is separated from every other client's data.</li>
				<li><b>No selling of data:</b> we do not sell your data or share it with third parties for marketing.</li>
				<li><b>Written confidentiality:</b> we commit to the confidentiality of your data in writing, in the offer and the contract.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>External channels and tools</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				Some systems run on external channels and tools (such as messaging apps, hosting providers and AI models),
				which are governed by their own policies. Your written offer names exactly which tools your project will use
				and what passes through them, before you agree.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<ul class="steps-plain">
				<li>Request a copy of your data, or have it corrected.</li>
				<li>Request deletion of your data when the relationship ends.</li>
				<li>Ask plainly and get a plain answer: what we see, what we do not see, and where your data is stored.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				For any data request, contact us through the official channels at the bottom of the page.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p class="section-sub" style="max-width:70ch">
				For any material change, we update this page and note the date of the latest update at the top.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

</BaseEn>
